# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# browser-automation artifacts (Playwright MCP snapshots, console logs, screenshots)
/.playwright-mcp/
/*.png

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# vercel
.vercel

# sanity — `sanity schema deploy` extracts a manifest here. Build output, not
# source; the schema itself lives in sanity/schemas/.
dist/

# Client source material and backups. These live in the repo root for
# convenience while the site is being built, but they are hundreds of megabytes
# each — GitHub rejects any file over 100MB, and a committed binary stays in
# history forever even after deletion. Keep them local.
*.tar.gz
CREATIVE STUDIO_Portfolio.pdf
CSI WEBSITE_PROJECT LIST.xlsx

# The client's raw project photography, as delivered: 81 full-resolution JPGs
# (20–49MB each, ~2GB total) plus write-ups, foldered by category. Staged here
# only so it is easy to browse while wiring up projects.
#
# It must never be committed. No single file trips GitHub's 100MB limit, so a
# push would SUCCEED and bolt 2GB into history permanently. It must also never
# ship in the build — everything under public/ is copied verbatim into the
# deployment and served unoptimized.
#
# The real destination is Sanity: project.coverImage and project.gallery are
# image assets served off Sanity's CDN. Once a project's photos are uploaded
# there, its folder here is redundant.
/public/02 - Projects*/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# AI-agent skills — installed per-developer, never part of the build.
#
# skills-lock.json IS committed and pins the exact source + hash of every
# skill, so these directories are reproducible the way node_modules is from
# package-lock.json. Reinstall both with:
#
#   npx skills@latest add jsmastery-pro/skills -a claude-code
#   npx skills@latest add sanity-io/agent-toolkit -a claude-code
#
# /.claude/  Claude Code skill installs (jsmastery-pro workflow skills +
#            a symlink to the Sanity skill)
# /.agents/  the generic copy other agents (Codex, etc.) read
/.agents/
/.claude/
.env*
